WEBVTT

00:00:11.095 --> 00:00:12.096
[groans]

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.016
<i>To a better future.</i>

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.770
In three weeks, my next-gen
MoonX rocket will blast off

00:00:19.854 --> 00:00:22.439
and deploy the Power Cell X3.

00:00:22.523 --> 00:00:23.524
That's right.

00:00:23.607 --> 00:00:28.028
Free wireless charging
from outer space directly to your phone.

00:00:28.112 --> 00:00:29.405
-[Wolf] Hey, guys.
-[Piranha] Hey.

00:00:29.488 --> 00:00:31.907
-Wolfie.
-Wolf! So you got the job?

00:00:31.991 --> 00:00:36.245
Well, I mean, it's not a hundred percent,
but he said... he said he'd call me.

00:00:36.328 --> 00:00:38.080
Well, you did better than Piranha.

00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:40.499
I thought I was supposed
to project confidence.

00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:42.293
-Yeah, but why a tuna?
-[purring]

00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:43.794
What? Tunas are confident.

00:00:43.878 --> 00:00:45.546
What tuna do you know
that's not confident?

00:00:45.629 --> 00:00:46.630
All of them.

00:00:46.714 --> 00:00:48.382
-Tunas are confident.
-[Piranha] Right?

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:50.467
Guys, come on. Life's like a car chase.

00:00:50.551 --> 00:00:51.552
You know what I mean?

00:00:51.635 --> 00:00:54.972
There's gonna be bumps in the road,
but when has that ever stopped us?

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.056
Never.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.558
It's just gonna take a little time.

00:00:57.641 --> 00:00:59.935
But I promise you,
people will come around.

00:01:00.019 --> 00:01:02.605
Even if we get framed
for the Phantom Bandit's crime spree?

00:01:02.688 --> 00:01:05.024
That's awfully specific.
Who's the Phantom--

00:01:05.107 --> 00:01:06.108
[stammers] Who?

00:01:06.191 --> 00:01:08.527
You haven't heard? It's all over the news.

00:01:08.611 --> 00:01:10.529
[narrator] There's a battle
of survival for the Bil--

00:01:10.613 --> 00:01:13.574
The Phantom Bandit hit
three locations yesterday,

00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:15.951
stealing several priceless artifacts.

00:01:16.035 --> 00:01:19.246
<i>The Phantom is known
for being impossible to trace,</i>

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:21.832
but this time, he left a calling card.

00:01:24.043 --> 00:01:26.545
-Wait, hey, hey. That's our move.
-Exactly.

00:01:26.629 --> 00:01:29.214
<i>Commissioner, are the Bad Guys
back to a life of crime</i>

00:01:29.298 --> 00:01:31.258
or are they being framed,

00:01:31.342 --> 00:01:33.844
Just like your face
with those fabulous bangs?

00:01:33.928 --> 00:01:35.387
Thank you. I cut them myself.

00:01:35.471 --> 00:01:38.140
Look, I cannot comment
on an ongoing investigation.

00:01:38.223 --> 00:01:41.769
But let's just say,
once a con, always a con.

00:01:41.852 --> 00:01:42.895
So it's the Bad Guys?

00:01:42.978 --> 00:01:44.688
[ Said no comment/!

00:01:44.772 --> 00:01:45.773
-Come on.
-What?

00:01:45.856 --> 00:01:47.983
How are we supposed to get a fresh start
when we get blamed

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:49.485
for every bad thing that happens?

00:01:49.568 --> 00:01:51.779
-[whirring, clattering]
-[dings]

00:01:51.862 --> 00:01:53.656
["Espresso” playing]

00:01:53.739 --> 00:01:55.032
Hey, guys.

00:01:55.616 --> 00:01:58.285
Isn't the sun particularly radiant today?

00:01:58.369 --> 00:01:59.662
What are you wearing?

00:01:59.745 --> 00:02:01.038
What are you drinking?

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:06.585
Wheatgrass kombucha with extra moss
and two shots of cold-pressed dandelion.

00:02:06.669 --> 00:02:10.798
Uh, I don't think you're
supposed to eat those things.

00:02:10.881 --> 00:02:12.883
Oh, you guys.

00:02:12.967 --> 00:02:15.928
I wish I could trade lighthearted japes
with you all night,

00:02:16.011 --> 00:02:17.930
but I'm late for Vinyasa.

00:02:18.013 --> 00:02:19.306
-Vinyasa?
-Wait, wait, wait.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:21.475
-You're going out?
-But you just got back.

00:02:21.558 --> 00:02:22.768
You know how it is.

00:02:22.851 --> 00:02:26.063
You think I got this body
by sitting around watching TV?

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:27.147
[Tarantula] Okay, ew.

00:02:27.231 --> 00:02:29.566
And don't wait up for me.
It's Lucha night.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:32.945
Well, bye!

00:02:33.028 --> 00:02:34.029
[dings]

00:02:37.533 --> 00:02:40.202
Guys, I think the kombucha ate his brain.

00:02:40.285 --> 00:02:43.163
Hey, you know what?
As long as he's happy, right?

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.582
And you're not?

00:02:45.666 --> 00:02:49.294
[grunts] I'd be happier
if I could land one of these jobs.

00:02:50.212 --> 00:02:51.964
[panting] First impressions
are hard to shake.

00:02:52.464 --> 00:02:53.716
Ooh, that was quick.

00:02:53.799 --> 00:02:55.426
I mean, when I first met you,

00:02:55.509 --> 00:02:58.512
I thought you were arrogant,
self-satisfied,

00:02:59.346 --> 00:03:00.681
dishonest,

00:03:00.764 --> 00:03:02.516
greedy for sure.

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:03.600
Oh, yeah?

00:03:04.101 --> 00:03:05.477
What changed your mind?

00:03:05.561 --> 00:03:06.687
What do you mean?

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.023
[chuckles] Very funny.

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:12.609
Seriously, it's hard to stay positive
when we keep getting rejected.

00:03:12.693 --> 00:03:15.112
It makes you feel, I don't know, hopeless.

00:03:15.738 --> 00:03:16.739
Hmm.

00:03:17.614 --> 00:03:20.701
I mean, going good
was the hardest thing that I ever did.

00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:24.038
And compared to you guys, I had it easy.

00:03:24.538 --> 00:03:27.583
No one ever knew
I was the Crimson Paw.

00:03:27.666 --> 00:03:31.336
I'm sorry. Did you say
you were the Crimson Paw--

00:03:32.713 --> 00:03:33.714
Sorry.

00:03:33.797 --> 00:03:35.674
-[Wolf grunts]
-I didn't quite catch that.

00:03:35.758 --> 00:03:37.176
[chuckling]

00:03:37.259 --> 00:03:40.429
Okay, you asked for it.

00:03:40.512 --> 00:03:44.892
You're about to discover
why they call me the Big, Bad Wo--

00:03:46.935 --> 00:03:48.771
[groaning]

00:03:50.898 --> 00:03:52.566
[distorted] I think I got carried away.

00:03:53.609 --> 00:03:56.820
I don't think this is
gonna help with my interviews.

00:03:56.904 --> 00:03:58.405
I don't know.

00:03:58.489 --> 00:04:01.492
I think it's cute. Gives you character.

00:04:01.575 --> 00:04:02.576
Oh.

00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:06.497
Do I have a concussion,
or is the governor flirting with me?

00:04:07.122 --> 00:04:08.123
Can't it be both?

00:04:08.207 --> 00:04:09.208
Hmm.

00:04:10.876 --> 00:04:11.877
-Uh...
-Oh.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.837
-Sorry. I shouldn't have...
-Oh, no, no, no.

00:04:13.921 --> 00:04:15.380
[stammers] I didn't really...

00:04:15.464 --> 00:04:16.882
Yeah, 'cause you're the governor,

00:04:16.965 --> 00:04:19.218
-and I'm, you know... Yeah.
-An ex-con.

00:04:19.301 --> 00:04:20.302
I know.

00:04:20.385 --> 00:04:22.054
-It's optics. [chuckles]
-Totally.

00:04:22.137 --> 00:04:24.389
-Let's just keep it friendly.
-Yeah, let's keep it friendly.

00:04:25.724 --> 00:04:27.392
-Medium friendly?
-Yeah.

00:04:27.476 --> 00:04:29.103
-[assistant] Madam Governor!
-Oops.

00:04:29.186 --> 00:04:30.354
[panting] Madam Governor,

00:04:30.437 --> 00:04:33.190
sorry to interrupt you
and your acquaintance.

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:34.608
Finally, she remembers my name.

00:04:34.691 --> 00:04:37.694
But you've got the children's
hospital fundraiser in 20 minutes.

00:04:37.778 --> 00:04:39.822
-I'll be right there, Maureen.
-Good. Thank you.

00:04:39.905 --> 00:04:42.741
Another fundraiser? Oof, look at you.

00:04:42.825 --> 00:04:44.493
Same time next week?

00:04:44.993 --> 00:04:46.954
My calendar's wide open.

00:04:48.789 --> 00:04:53.794
Hey, I know it's tough,
but you can't lose hope, okay?

00:04:53.877 --> 00:04:55.629
People do want to trust you.

00:04:55.712 --> 00:04:58.006
You just have to give them a reason.

00:04:59.383 --> 00:05:00.384
Promise?

00:05:00.968 --> 00:05:02.302
Governor's word.

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:06.431
But until then, I would
work on that right hook.

00:05:06.515 --> 00:05:09.184
It feels a little like
I'm getting kissed by a butterfly.

00:05:09.893 --> 00:05:11.353
Catch you later, tough guy.

00:05:11.436 --> 00:05:14.189
I was holding back. [chuckles, groans]

00:05:16.441 --> 00:05:17.442
[grunts]

00:05:26.827 --> 00:05:29.705
Huh. "Give 'em a reason."

00:05:30.914 --> 00:05:34.251
No! I said no comment.

00:05:34.835 --> 00:05:35.836
[grunts]

00:05:36.378 --> 00:05:37.921
I want answers.

00:05:38.005 --> 00:05:40.299
Get me security footage,
scour the phone logs,

00:05:40.382 --> 00:05:41.800
and where's my coffee?

00:05:42.301 --> 00:05:43.844
-Uh, Commissioner?
-Not now.

00:05:43.927 --> 00:05:44.928
But you have a visitor.

00:05:45.012 --> 00:05:46.722
-They can wait.
-[deputy] Uh, but he's--

00:05:46.805 --> 00:05:47.806
Hey, hey, Chief.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:49.349
[coughs]

00:05:49.433 --> 00:05:51.852
Can I just say, love the bangs.

00:05:51.935 --> 00:05:54.563
First off, it's "Commissioner" now.

00:05:54.646 --> 00:05:55.981
-And second--
-Ooh, nice.

00:05:56.064 --> 00:05:57.065
What's the difference?

00:05:57.149 --> 00:05:59.818
Well, the chief is the top
uniformed officer, whereas--

00:05:59.902 --> 00:06:02.154
Why am I explaining this to you?

00:06:02.237 --> 00:06:04.698
[gasps] Did you touch my board?

00:06:04.781 --> 00:06:06.575
My board. My beautiful board.

00:06:06.658 --> 00:06:10.370
Oh, I'm sorry.
I thought I heard it say, "Solve me."

00:06:10.454 --> 00:06:11.955
[grunts] Wolf.

00:06:12.039 --> 00:06:15.334
Listen, I think we're both having
an optics problem.

00:06:15.417 --> 00:06:16.627
You need to show the world

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:18.712
you've got this investigation
under control,

00:06:18.795 --> 00:06:20.589
and we need to show the world we're good.

00:06:20.672 --> 00:06:22.633
If I help you catch the Bandit,
it's a win-win.

00:06:22.716 --> 00:06:23.717
I'm calling the governor.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.303
Go ahead. It was basically her idea.

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:27.971
-[groans]
-Look at this.

00:06:28.055 --> 00:06:31.141
Each of the robberies occurred
within a three-minute window.

00:06:31.225 --> 00:06:32.226
So?

00:06:32.309 --> 00:06:35.187
Three minutes is the loop rate
of most standard security consoles,

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:37.064
which means whoever did this...

00:06:37.147 --> 00:06:39.691
Patched into security from the inside.

00:06:39.775 --> 00:06:41.109
Bingo.

00:06:41.193 --> 00:06:44.112
[groans] Fine. Let's say they did.

00:06:44.196 --> 00:06:46.323
How would we even trace that?

00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:48.992
We'd need some kind
of high-tech computer expert.

00:06:50.369 --> 00:06:51.912
They'd have had to clone the IP address

00:06:51.995 --> 00:06:54.915
and redirect the feed
to a four gigahertz dummy console, duh.

00:06:54.998 --> 00:06:55.999
Huh?

00:06:56.083 --> 00:06:59.878
Your Bandit is clever,
but not as clever as he thinks he is.

00:06:59.962 --> 00:07:02.756
However, he'd still need an inside man.

00:07:04.383 --> 00:07:05.550
Hmm.

00:07:05.634 --> 00:07:06.635
Hey!

00:07:07.511 --> 00:07:08.512
Hold this.

00:07:09.096 --> 00:07:10.722
Hmm. [muttering]

00:07:11.723 --> 00:07:12.724
There!

00:07:13.684 --> 00:07:14.768
But that's just the janitor.

00:07:14.851 --> 00:07:16.979
Perhaps to the untrained eye,

00:07:17.062 --> 00:07:19.439
but if he's really just the janitor,

00:07:19.523 --> 00:07:23.318
why is he pushing
around an empty bucket, hmm?

00:07:24.361 --> 00:07:27.990
So the real question is,
how did he get in?

00:07:28.073 --> 00:07:29.283
[groans]

00:07:30.951 --> 00:07:34.413
[Piranha] I'd come this way, jam the fan,
pop the grate and bam, you're in.

00:07:34.496 --> 00:07:35.747
Ooh, ugh.

00:07:37.082 --> 00:07:38.292
Why is there pickles in this?

00:07:38.875 --> 00:07:40.794
Because that's my lunch.

00:07:40.877 --> 00:07:42.671
Who said you could eat my lunch?

00:07:42.754 --> 00:07:43.797
He said there was lunch.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:45.716
Chief, come on. Let's focus.

00:07:45.799 --> 00:07:47.718
So we know when and we know how.

00:07:47.801 --> 00:07:50.304
The real question is why.

